From 910d0f769150e520a622bf19918eb117ed95547e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cstech-05 <cstech-05@CS-MBP-05.local>
Date: Thu, 12 Feb 2026 12:58:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add H.265 support and MongoDB integration for VMAF tracking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add dual codec support (H.264 + H.265) for video transcoding
- H.265 streams use 40% less bitrate for similar quality
- Generate 6 video variants (720p, 480p, 1080p × 2 codecs)
- Add m3u8_link field to MongoDB schema for HLS manifest URLs
- Add codec field to MongoDB to distinguish h264/h265 variants
- Auto-generate public m3u8 URLs from transcoding output
- Update VMAF calculator to store m3u8_link and codec in MongoDB
- Add --m3u8-link and --codec CLI arguments to run_vmaf.py

This enables better compression with H.265 while maintaining H.264
compatibility, and provides full tracking of streaming URLs and
codec variants in MongoDB for quality analysis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
